<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 03, 2004 - 2:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I remember the message boards about the Baton Rouge Serial killer.  People thought he was monitoring the internet for news and messages about him, and all sorts of stuff.  Turns out he wasn&#39;t online at all.  It is my considered opinion that this BTK isn&#39;t online, and prefers the old method of reading the paper and probably clipping the articles about him.  <BR> <BR>I dont&#39; think he grew with the times, he probalby doesn&#39;t have a DVD player, or a computer.. He lives in the past, stunted, and lonely. He wants fame.   <BR> <BR>Either that, or it&#39;s a clever hoaxter, trying to boost future book sales. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
