<!--Post: 1165--><!--Time: 1097523434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1165"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->nobody<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, October 11, 2004 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->once there was a child who had no friends.  the child craved attention like no one else could imagine.  all they wanted to do was have someone, anyone like them. <BR> <BR>in order to get attention, they came up with outrageous stories to tell.  they spent every cent they had on interesting things just so others would talk to them. <BR> <BR>the child grew up, still lonely. it is hard when no one else understands you or even tries. <BR> <BR>try living in a world with no one to turn to.  even when it seems as if there are plenty of people around to love, you are still close to no one.  no one truly knows you. <BR> <BR>the difference between me and you, btk, is i didn&#39;t kill anyone.  i learned to live with my circumstances, even those beyond my control.  i took out my aggression in other areas that hurt no one else. <BR> <BR>i know what it is like to be different.  i know what it is like to feel no one cares.  i know what it is like to dread waking up to the same routine every single day.  i know what it is like waking up to the same name every single day. <BR> <BR>yet i didn&#39;t hurt anyone. <BR>yet i didn&#39;t kill anyone. <BR> <BR>you&#39;re misunderstood.  everyone tries to put you into such a tiny box and that is why you&#39;re still out there.  you&#39;re not just a murderer.  you&#39;re much more than that -- you&#39;re a person too. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1165-->
<!--Post: 1170--><!--Time: 1097530225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chris Greenacre<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, October 11, 2004 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Make sure you give us a face to that very ordinary voice one day! <BR>I reckon you&#39;ve played your last season sir, but there&#39;s only one way you&#39;ll make the all time greats squad. <BR> <BR>Reveal yourself. <BR> <BR>My love goes out to all those lost and their suffering families, xx. <BR> <BR>Even though you fascinate me sir, I wish you never had existed. <BR> <BR>Chris Greenacre.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
