<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1564"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 02, 2004 - 4:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To the killer: <BR>On the off chance you really DO read all this stuff we wanabes write I hope you are able to appreciate the irony. You have worked off and on for decades to get into the minds and fears of everyone in Wichita, to make your name whispered and feared.  Now, you have succeeded.  Every patron of the library will take a glance at every middle aged man there and wonder.  Every Fed-Ex employee will pause as they open their drop box.  When the phone rings at KAKE the secretary will wonder if it could be you.  The man going to the mailbox will wonder, &#34;Is that him, mailing another letter to the Eagle?&#34;.  You have implanted your legend in the consciousness of the entire community.   <BR>And that&#39;s the irony.  Now that leading on everybody in the city is really getting fun, you can&#39;t do it anymore. No matter what method you would use to communicate with authorities, the press or the public you can never feel it is safe.  Everyone is too vigilant now.  Any attempt on your part would only result in constant watching over your shoulder and sleepless nights worrying that someone did see you.  How many places are being watched?  No matter how out of the way, are you SURE there is not a camera somewhere? <BR>The irony is that you have beaten yourself at your own game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1564-->
<!--Post: 1569--><!--Time: 1102057292-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1569"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 02, 2004 - 11:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK, <BR>Your hero, Zodiac, had the guts to send letters to two major US cities, San Francisco and Los Angeles. The reason you won&#39;t send anything anywhere outside of Wichita is quite simple: you&#39;d be caught. Zodiac was original, you aren&#39;t. Your letters are embarrassingly naive and fifth-rate, you instill no fear; we laugh at you. You are a failure and a coward, and no one hears your footsteps: your tread is the walk of a dead man. <i>And you know it</i>.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1569-->
