<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1579"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lawrence Bittaker<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 03, 2004 - 7:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK: I had the Gender Genie analyze the following poem of yours, and it determined it was written by a WOMAN - which suggests you have a female partner acting with you, at least in regard to the poems. Serial killers who have knowledgeable/participatory female partners is not unknown, as you should know, Gerald and Charlene Gallegos and the Lonely Hearts Killers being just two examples.  <BR> <BR> <BR>Oh, Anna Why Didn&#39;t You Appear <BR> <BR>T&#39; was perfect plan of deviant pleasure so bold on that Spring niteMy inner felling hot with propension of the new awakening season <BR> <BR>Warn, wet with inner fear and rapture, my pleasure of entanglement,like new vines at night <BR> <BR>Oh, Anna, Why Didn&#39;t You AppearDrop of fear fresh Spring rain would roll down from your nakednessto scent to lofty fever that burns within, <BR> <BR>In that small world of longing, fear, rapture, and desparation,the game we play, fall on devil earsFantasy spring forth, mounts, to storm fury, then winter clam atthe end. <BR> <BR>Oh, Anna Why Didn&#39;t You AppearAlone, now in another time span I lay with sweet enrapture garmentsacross most private thought <BR> <BR>Bed of Spring moist grass, clean before the sun, enslaved withcontrol, warm wind scenting the air, sun light sparkle tearsin eyes so deep and clear. <BR> <BR>Alone again I trod in pass memory of mirrors, and ponder why fornumber eight was not. <BR> <BR>Oh, Anna Why Didn&#39;t You Appear <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
