<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1835"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rusty_gate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rusty_gate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 5:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if Anna ever wakes up in the middle of the night, thoughts of you slip by her like the warm breeze of a cold chill. She probably only imagines a glimpse of that mirror you hide so cleverly, you yourself never really seeing it clearly. And to think you were so close, with only garments to show for all your painstakes. You reinact the rapture and entaglement that brings you closer to the answer, a step closer to sneaking through the gate, but number eight was not. You wont be satisfied until you lure another soul into that  corner and they are at your mercy, scared, fearful, longing for an answer in a world you create for them, where you are God and they are under your control. But your not, are you. The only thing you&#39;ve managed to control is the tears that sparkle in the sun light as you drain the life out of them, and then it ends <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
