<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sam<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 4:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK why don&#39;t you ask KWYA why she/he hasn&#39;t turned you in to the police. I mean IF they know who you are all they have to do is advise the police. <BR>I&#39;m sure IF all the lines connect police would have NO problem obtaining your dna. It&#39;s called evidenuary search warrent. So Know who you Are were waiting for you to drop the dime.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
