<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1970"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->ElectraQTKitty<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 7:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK <BR> <BR>I highly doubt that you&#39;re reading this, but hey, stranger things have happened.  <BR> <BR>So, you&#39;ve decided to make a comeback. I&#39;m assuming that you&#39;ve missed having the attention of everyone. Attention, or fear, I don&#39;t know which. I highly doubt that you&#39;re going to strike again. Thirty years can really slow a person down, and a normal person around your age starts to forget things, imagine what that does to a person with &#34;demons&#34;. A slow forgetful crazed old man, usually doesnt get away with much. <BR> <BR>Is this comeback just a cry for attention, or is it a build-up of guilt? I doubt it&#39;s guilt, you&#39;re too messed up to feel compassion. I hope that these innocent people haunt you.  <BR> <BR>Keep playing these games instead of just coming out and saying &#34;it&#39;s me!&#34;, but I suggest that you keep a written confession note in your wallet so that when you do die, we know it&#39;s you, and that we don&#39;t credit everything you&#39;ve done to a copycat. It seems like your crimes are all you&#39;ve got. <BR> <BR>You should just turn yourself in. Do it, not because it&#39;s right, do it so you can protect what you&#39;ve done.  <BR> <BR>Either way, you&#39;re a sad loser. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1970-->
