</a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 1:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Continued from previous post. <BR> <BR>Also BTK, I wrote a poem for you &#40;not for the reasons others here do, like to show you they understand you, emphathize with you, want to be your friend, want to be your confessional, or want to make love to you&#41;. I hope the webmaster allows it. It contains no profanity, just a vision of how BTK&#39;s life will end based on the type of person he is: <BR> <BR>Roses are red, <BR>Violets are blue. <BR>Ha ha! Anna got away from you! <BR> <BR>Your corpse decays on a couch, <BR>Discovered by a concerned mailman. <BR>In no great surprise, dead there you lay, <BR>With your penis firmly in hand. <BR> <BR>Your power lies limp, <BR>The driving force of your shame. <BR>BTK you do realize, <BR>You will never live - or kill - again? <BR> <BR>A mystery you shall remain, <BR>But BTK, you must know it&#39;s true: <BR>Although reviled for your disbursement of pain, <BR>Society neither fears nor worships you. <BR> <BR>Did you appear normal, or more like a freak? <BR>Did you live like a king, or a bum on the street? <BR> <BR>You lived in shame and fear, <BR>Intent never to let your secret out. <BR>Enjoying your controlling of society, <BR>BTK, we tire of you, please die and sign out. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
